        "id": 68499,
        "name": "Pydro",
        "username": "Pydro",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-07-18T18:04:16.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Greywind\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/greywind/48/2006_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Greywind:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Air freezes water, which leads to the breakdown/erosion on the earth. There are places where the rocks have been carved by the winds.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>There are many more places where water destroys earth. It also doesn't explain what earth does to air.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Magic can do anything!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I have no problem with this answer, but there shouldn't be an ssumption that it makes sense. If a fireball takes out water, then a lightning bolt shouldn't have a special effect on water either. Either maintain logic, or throw it out the window completely.</p>",
